 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Do the same to both sides to keep the equation balanced.</li><li>Collect the x terms on one side and the numbers on the other: 5x − 3 = 2x + 9 → 3x = 12 → x = 4.</li><li>Expand brackets first. With fractions, multiply both sides by the denominator.</li><li>Check by substituting the answer.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>3(x − 2) = x + 8</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>3x − 6 = x + 8</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>2x = 14</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 7</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The sign when moving</td><td>Subtract 2x from both sides; the sign changes.</td></tr><tr><td>Part of a bracket</td><td>Multiply every term.</td></tr><tr><td>One side only</td><td>Multiply both sides by the denominator.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
